WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.350
July is quickly shaping up to be the hottest
month of the year, and we're not talking about

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:05.350
the weather.

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:09.930
Netflix's upcoming release schedule is a firestorm
of hot new movies and shows.

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:14.440
From bingeable new seasons of fan-favorite
shows to great new Netflix original horror

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:18.060
thrillers, there's definitely a lot to get
excited about in the upcoming weeks.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.960
Here are all the new movies and shows coming
to Netflix in July 2018.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.460
The Legacy of a Whitetail Deer Hunter

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:30.230
From Danny McBride and Jody Hill, the duo
behind HBO's Vice Principals, The Legacy of

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:35.670
a Whitetail Deer Hunter follows aging hunting
legend and TV personality Buck Ferguson as

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:39.989
he heads up into the mountains to reconnect
with his son… with Buck's cameraman, Don,

00:00:39.989 --> 00:00:40.989
tagging along.

00:00:40.989 --> 00:00:43.210
"Well, it HAS been two years, I dunno..."

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:44.730
"What you a human calendar?

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:45.730
Mr. Trapper Keeper.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:48.390
I know how long it's been."

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:50.089
Sacred Games: Season 1

00:00:50.089 --> 00:00:54.809
As India's first Netflix original series,
Sacred Games continues the service's M.O.

00:00:54.809 --> 00:00:57.929
of bringing international talent onto their
diverse lineup.

00:00:57.929 --> 00:01:02.289
The show is described as a dark crime thriller
and is based on the bestselling novel of the

00:01:02.289 --> 00:01:03.620
same name.

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:06.409
Samantha: Season 1

00:01:06.409 --> 00:01:10.310
Netflix made a great decision when they brought
on Brazilian series 3%, and it looks like

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:13.590
they're intent on tapping the country for
even more of its programming.

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:18.490
Samantha is an upcoming Brazilian show about
a former '80s child star who's desperate to

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:23.009
reach the level of fame she once had, leading
her on some wild adventures as she does everything

00:01:23.009 --> 00:01:25.950
in her power to get back into the spotlight.

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:28.159
Somebody Feed Phil: The Second Course

00:01:28.159 --> 00:01:32.450
Most people probably know Phil Rosenthal as
the creator of the long-running sitcom hit

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:36.789
Everybody Loves Raymond, but in recent years,
he's been on a different sort of adventure.

00:01:36.789 --> 00:01:41.369
In Somebody Feed Phil, Rosenthal jets off
to exotic locations to check out the local

00:01:41.369 --> 00:01:42.600
culture and cuisine.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:46.799
Basically, it's like every other travel food
show, with the distinction that Rosenthal

00:01:46.799 --> 00:01:49.620
isn't an expert on either culture or cuisine.

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:51.000
He's just a guy who just likes food.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.079
"Nothing wrong with that.

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:56.179
And you know we like anything on a stick."

00:01:56.179 --> 00:01:58.780
Comedians in Cars Getting Coffee: Freshly
Brewed

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:03.750
Jerry Seinfeld's undemanding talk show Comedians
in Cars Getting Coffee is rolling back into

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:07.210
Netflix with a freshly brewed batch of today's
hottest comedians.

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:11.730
The series' fifth collection, "Freshly Brewed,"
will see Seinfeld chatting with Dave Chappelle,

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:15.659
Kate McKinnon, and Zach Galifianakis, to name
a few.

00:02:15.659 --> 00:02:18.300
First Team: Juventus: Season 1: Part B

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:23.840
Sports fans had a ball with the first part
of Netflix's 2018 docu-series First Team:

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:29.209
Juventus, which follows the Juventus football
club during their 2017 to 2018 season.

00:02:29.209 --> 00:02:33.430
Each 40-minute episode goes behind the scenes
to take an intimate look of the players and

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:36.060
coaches of the Italian soccer team.

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:38.980
Inside the World’s Toughest Prisons: Season
2

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:43.470
They may not be too deadly to safely get a
camera crew inside, but the prisons that journalist

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:48.090
Paul Connolly visits in Inside the World's
Toughest Prisons definitely reek of danger.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:52.610
In the first season, Connolly posed as a prisoner
in four separate lockups around the world,

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:55.220
living face to face with dangerous inmates.

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:59.250
Season 2 will see the same approach with a
new presenter - Raphael Rowe, a journalist

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:02.819
who himself actually spent 12 years in prison.

00:03:02.819 --> 00:03:04.349
The Skin of The Wolf

00:03:04.349 --> 00:03:09.269
This Spanish movie made its U.S. premiere
in March 2018 at the Miami Film Festival.

00:03:09.269 --> 00:03:13.340
The story follows a lonely hunter who's the
last remaining resident of an abandoned town

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:14.390
at the top of a mountain.

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:18.340
Don't let the Spanish subtitles hold you back,
because there aren't many lines to read - The

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:22.409
Skin of the Wolf features precious little
dialogue, with long stretches containing none

00:03:22.409 --> 00:03:23.409
at all.

00:03:23.409 --> 00:03:28.400
Yet there's a raw, hypnotic quality to the
film that keeps it from getting boring.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:29.480
White Fang

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:33.549
Netflix's newest animated film is bringing
Jack London's timeless tale to a whole new

00:03:33.549 --> 00:03:34.549
audience.

00:03:34.549 --> 00:03:38.060
Like the book, the narrative of the film is
told from the perspective of White Fang, a

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:43.069
half-wolf sled dog who's adopted by a Native
American tribe and learns to become a vicious

00:03:43.069 --> 00:03:44.069
fighter.

00:03:44.069 --> 00:03:47.849
Nick Offerman, Paul Giamatti, and Rashida
Jones lend their voices to the cast.

00:03:47.849 --> 00:03:52.569
Make sure you check out The Legacy of a Whitetail
Deer Hunter, Sacred Games Season 1, Samantha

00:03:52.569 --> 00:03:57.701
Season 1, Somebody Feed Phil: The Second Course,
Comedians in Cars Getting Coffee: Freshly

00:03:57.701 --> 00:04:02.731
Brewed, First Team: Juventus, Inside the World's
Toughest Prisons: Season 2, The Skin of the

00:04:02.731 --> 00:04:08.060
Wolf, and White Fang when they drop onto Netflix
on July 6.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:09.060
Drug Lords: Season 2

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:13.780
A look at the most notorious criminal kingpins
in history, Drug Lords hones in on famous

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:18.850
names like Pablo Escobar, Frank Lucas, and
Kath Pettingill, dubbed "Granny Evil" for

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:21.419
her iron grip on the Melbourne drug trade.

00:04:21.419 --> 00:04:25.410
Season 2 will raise the stakes with even more
of the head honchos of crime, from El Chapo

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.590
to Jamaican gangster Christopher Coke.

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:30.539
Look for it on July 10th.

00:04:30.539 --> 00:04:31.539
How it Ends

00:04:31.539 --> 00:04:35.990
Starring Theo James and Forest Whitaker, How
it Ends is an action thriller that follows

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:40.180
a man who sets off on a journey across the
country to find his pregnant girlfriend after

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:42.270
a mysterious apocalyptic event.

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:45.190
Check it out on July 13th.

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:46.190
Sugar Rush

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:50.780
Netflix has been piling on the cooking shows
lately, with Nailed It and Ugly Delicious

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:52.770
premiering in early 2018.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:54.840
Now Sugar Rush is joining the roster.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:59.880
In this cooking competition, chef Adriano
Zumbo and bakery owner Candace Nelson judge

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:03.910
participants who are racing against the clock
to whip up the best desserts.

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:08.020
It should be a sweet time, and you can catch
it all on July 13th.

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:10.000
Bonus Family: Season 2

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:14.650
In this Swedish series, family takes center
stage as two divorcees with kids move in with

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:17.770
each other… and bring all their emotional
baggage with them.

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:21.780
With everybody living under the same roof,
there's bound to be plenty of drama and comedy

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:22.780
alike.

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:25.810
Take a look at Season 2 when it drops on July
15th.

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:28.290
The Joel McHale Show with Joel McHale: Part
2

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:32.919
While Joel McHale's green-screened celebrity
rants originally aired as weekly episodes,

00:05:32.919 --> 00:05:36.160
Netflix is changing up the format for the
next batch, dropping them all on the same

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:37.160
day.

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:41.830
The series sees Community star Joel McHale
poking fun at popular shows, reality TV, and

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:44.630
celebrities, interspersed with scripted comedy
bits.

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:48.050
Look for Part 2 to land on July 15th.

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:49.550
Amazing Interiors

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:53.850
With The World's Most Extraordinary Homes,
Netflix took viewers on a whirlwind tour around

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:57.400
the globe to visit a few of the craziest looking
homes in existence.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:02.060
With Amazing Interiors, the format continues
- only this time, the crazy is all inside.

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:05.090
What will you find when you walk through the
doors of these homes?

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:08.180
Find out on July 20th.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.190
Dark Tourist

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:13.590
Instead of visiting the usual cultural highlights
around the world, Dark Tourist pinpoints the

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:19.280
planet's most morbid settings, such as abandoned
nuclear reactors and haunted forests.

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:23.669
Journalist and filmmaker David Farrier leads
the charge, promising a weird journey into

00:06:23.669 --> 00:06:24.930
the unexpected.

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:28.009
Take the plunge on July 20th.

00:06:28.009 --> 00:06:29.009
Father of the Year

00:06:29.009 --> 00:06:33.610
David Spade headlines this coming-of-age comedy,
which sees two boys coming home from college.

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:37.221
When they get into an argument about who's
father could beat up the other's father, one

00:06:37.221 --> 00:06:39.289
of their dads steps up to the challenge.

00:06:39.289 --> 00:06:40.590
Hijinks ensue.

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:43.540
Take a look on July 20th.

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:44.910
Last Chance U

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:49.139
For two seasons, Netflix tagged along as the
troubled teens of East Mississippi Community

00:06:49.139 --> 00:06:54.879
College, or EMCC, fought to return to Division
1 status and achieve their football dreams.

00:06:54.879 --> 00:07:00.080
Nicknamed Last Chance U, EMCC offered many
of these players their last shot at redemption.

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:03.240
For the third season, Netflix is releasing
a two-parter.

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:07.849
The first takes a look at the players who
left EMCC after the first two seasons and

00:07:07.849 --> 00:07:11.740
is called, appropriately, Last Chance U: EMCC
&amp; Life After.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:16.879
The second - Last Chance U: INDY: Part 1 - starts
up the new season at a new school: Independence

00:07:16.879 --> 00:07:18.710
Community College in Kansas.

00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:21.819
The expectations are lower, but the stakes
are higher than ever.

00:07:21.819 --> 00:07:25.070
Look for both to land on July 20th.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:26.250
The Warning

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:29.080
Keep your eyes peeled for Spanish thriller
The Warning.

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:32.680
When a ten-year-old boy finds a note in a
gas station that seems to predict his death,

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:36.410
he'll have to team up with a mysterious stranger
to figure out what's going on before it's

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:37.410
too late.

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:42.560
Get ready for all the twists and turns when
The Warning shows up on July 24th.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:43.560
Extinction

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:47.540
This sci-fi thriller stars Michael Pena as
a father who's recurring nightmares about

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:49.639
an alien invasion come true.

00:07:49.639 --> 00:07:53.320
When actual aliens attack the planet, he'll
have to fight to keep his family safe from

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:54.780
the extraterrestrial threat.

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:57.470
Lizzy Caplan and Luke Cage's Mike Colter co-star.

00:07:57.470 --> 00:07:59.740
Look for Extinction on July 27th.

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:02.870
Roman Empire: Reign of Blood: Master of Rome

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:07.830
Netflix's docu-drama series Roman Empire:
Reign of Blood has spent two years thrilling

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:11.070
fans with its historical look at the beginnings
of the fall of Rome.

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:15.220
The series uses actors and sets to play out
the drama, while the occasional voiceover

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:19.520
or talking head pops in to provide documentary-style
commentary on what's going on.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:23.980
The upcoming Roman Empire: Reign of Blood:
Master of Rome will follow the same format,

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:26.550
and this time, the focus is on Julius Caesar.

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:29.280
Queue it up on July 27th.

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:31.729
Orange is the New Black: Season 6

00:08:31.729 --> 00:08:35.830
For five seasons, Piper and her friends have
regaled audiences in one of the most engaging

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:38.040
and original shows in recent memory.

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:42.250
We've seen relationships form, flourish and
wither, all within the halls of Litchfield

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:43.250
prison.

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:46.980
Judging by the brief teaser for the new season,
the show will pick up right where fans last

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:50.590
saw Piper and the remaining inmates in the
Season 5 cliffhanger.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:53.640
Look for it on July 27th.

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:54.680
The Bleeding Edge

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:58.830
Through candid interviews with patients and
medical professionals, The Bleeding Edge paints

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:03.920
a terrifying picture of medical devices rushed
through safety testing and installed in hospitals

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:05.250
across the country.

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:09.160
There's nothing more terrifying than a medical
horror story, so it's sure to be an eye-opening

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:10.160
experience.

00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:12.430
Take a look on July 27th.

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:14.900
A Very Secret Service: Season 2

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:18.460
This goofy spy comedy is sort of like the
French answer to Get Smart.

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:22.910
With both hard-hitting drama and absurd comedy,
the first season of A Very Secret Service

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:25.070
built a loyal - if small - fan base.

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:27.450
The second season promises more of the same.

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:30.940
Don't miss it when it arrives on Netflix on
July 30th.

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:33.610
Terrace House: Opening New Doors: Part 3

00:09:33.610 --> 00:09:37.850
Inexplicably one of Netflix's more popular
shows, Terrace House operates on the basic

00:09:37.850 --> 00:09:42.290
premise that a reality show doesn't need any
scripting whatsoever to draw in viewers.

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:47.190
This Japanese series is low key, drama free,
and utterly hypnotizing for no discernible

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:48.190
reason.

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:52.980
Part 3 of the spinoff Opening New Doors hits
on July 31st.

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:55.040
Original stand-up comedy

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:57.630
Netflix is offering a different take on comedy
this July.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:02.470
In addition to two full-length specials, Netflix
is also releasing a stand-up collection titled

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:06.770
The Comedy Lineup, which will see multiple
comedians take the stage for short sets.

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:11.350
That shows up on July 3rd, and you also can
catch Jim Jefferies: This Is Me Now on July

00:10:11.350 --> 00:10:15.750
13th, followed by Iliza Shlesinger : Elder
Millennial on July 24th.

00:10:15.750 --> 00:10:21.010
That wraps up all the Netflix originals arriving
in July 2018, so let's turn to everything

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:25.090
else being added to the streaming service
next month.

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:26.340
New movies

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:30.960
As far as Netflix is concerned, blockbuster
season officially begins on July 1st.

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:35.280
The first of the month will dawn with classic
action films like the Jurassic Park trilogy,

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:37.290
The Boondock Saints, and Van Helsing.

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:42.330
July 1st will also see the arrival of some
great dramas, such as Menace II Society, and

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:43.360
We Own the Night.

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:46.960
Later in the month, you can look for Blue
Valentine on the 5th, Gone Baby Gone on the

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:48.710
12th, and Her on the 29th.

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:53.630
For laughs, don't miss Ryan Reynolds' 2014
dark comedy The Voices, which sees Reynolds

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:56.000
as a slightly psychopathic blue collar worker.

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:57.810
"You know I'm a talking cat.

00:10:57.810 --> 00:10:59.120
There's no such thing.

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:01.850
Everything I say, is really you."

00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:03.260
"That's true buddy.

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:04.670
It's all you."

00:11:04.670 --> 00:11:05.670
"Whaaaaaaaat?"

00:11:05.670 --> 00:11:09.640
That's arriving on the first, alongside the
return of Bo Burnham's stand-up special what.

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:13.110
Finally, Kevin Hart: Let Me Explain is dropping
on the 13th.

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:16.740
Netflix is also rolling out plenty of options
for the family to watch together.

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:21.700
Look for Finding Neverland, the two Scooby-Doo
movies, and The Princess Diaries on July 1st,

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:23.980
followed by Disney's Bolt on the 22nd.

00:11:23.980 --> 00:11:27.930
Unfortunately, July is going to be slim pickings
for the horror fans in the room.

00:11:27.930 --> 00:11:33.130
There are only two upcoming films on the docket:
Deceived arrives on July 1st, and Scream 4

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:35.560
arrives on July 7th.

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:36.560
New television

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:40.630
If Netflix is coming up short in some of their
movie categories, they're more than making

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:42.850
up for it with their television selection.

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:48.390
You can escape the summer heat with new seasons
of Blue Bloods, Hawaii Five-O, NCIS, and Madam

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:50.040
Secretary on the first.

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:54.980
July 2nd sees the arrival of Season 4 of The
Good Witch and Season 1 of The Sinner, and

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:58.550
July 6 will herald the addition of The Fosters:
Season 5.

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:03.420
Finally, July 28th will bring the dysfunctional
Gallagher family back home as Season 8 of

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:04.550
Shameless arrives.

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:05.960
Thanks for watching!

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:08.630
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:10.830
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

